# The asset-LOD study's forced-rung and dolly arms (ADR-348).
#
# `tools/make_assetlod_arms.py` writes 61 projects and their scenes here, about a megabyte of
# generated JSON. Two kinds of them are tracked and the rest are not.
#
# **Tracked**: `_arm-*` (the control experiment that asks whether the tree is what costs at all) and
# `tree-<view>-off` / `tree-<view>-auto` (the before/after pairs the ADR's performance table is
# built from). Those are the ones somebody reading the record would want to open.
#
# **Ignored**: `tree-<view>-r<n>` and `dolly-*`. They exist only as inputs to two `[.analysis]`
# instruments that skip cleanly without them, they are 100 files of near-identical JSON, and one
# command remakes every one of them byte-for-byte:
#
#     tools/make_assetlod_arms.py
tree-*-r1.json
tree-*-r1.scene.json
tree-*-r2.json
tree-*-r2.scene.json
tree-*-r3.json
tree-*-r3.scene.json
tree-*-r4.json
tree-*-r4.scene.json
tree-*-r2-nothin.json
tree-*-r2-nothin.scene.json
dolly-*.json
dolly-*.scene.json

# The ADR-354 measurement arms: `floor-*` (the maxScreenError ladder the 16 px choice was rendered
# from) and `perf-*` (the before/after matrix). Each is the shipping Tree of Life scene with exactly
# one key changed on its five tree nodes, so the ADR's table states everything needed to remake
# them:
#
#   floor-off        no `lod` block
#   floor-NN         "lod": { "enabled": true, "maxScreenError": NN.0 }
#   perf-<scene>-lodoff / -lodon   the named scene with the block removed / set to 16.0
#
# Twenty files of 700-line JSON differing by one line each is not worth carrying, and the previous
# round of this already cost the branch 48,000 lines of generated data before it was trimmed.
floor-*.json
floor-*.scene.json
perf-*.json
perf-*.scene.json
